# Each entry needs a justification in docs/security.md. Nothing gets ignored
# silently.

# AVD-AWS-0010 - CloudFront access logging. Standard logging v1 needs S3 ACLs,
# which conflict with the BucketOwnerEnforced ownership this project enforces;
# v2 adds recurring CloudWatch ingestion cost. Deferred, documented.
AVD-AWS-0010

# AVD-AWS-0011 - WAF on the distribution. USD 5/month per Web ACL before a
# single request; out of scope for a personal project.
AVD-AWS-0011

# AVD-AWS-0089 - S3 server access logging on the site bucket. Nothing reaches
# the bucket except CloudFront over OAC, and API access logs already capture
# the request path that matters.
AVD-AWS-0089

# AVD-AWS-0132 - S3 bucket does not use a customer-managed KMS key. Same
# control as Checkov CKV_AWS_145, already accepted: SSE-KMS behind CloudFront
# OAC needs a key policy granting the CloudFront service principal
# kms:Decrypt, and bills a KMS request on every cache miss. The state bucket,
# where it matters, does use SSE-KMS.
AVD-AWS-0132
AWS-0132
